ENSv2:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/overview

Permissioned Registry:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/permissioned-registry

Permissioned Resolver:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/permissioned-resolver

Enhanced Access Control:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/enhanced-access-control

Contract Developer Guide:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/tutorial-contract-developers

App Developer Guide:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensv2/tutorial-app-developers

ENSIP-25:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensip/25/

ENSIP-26:
https://docs.ens.domains/ensip/26/

MANDATORY

Before implementing ENSv2 functionality:

1. Read the relevant current official documentation.
2. Verify the current Sepolia deployment/interfaces.
3. Verify the exact registry/resolver/access-control APIs.
4. Do not rely on old ENSv1 patterns when ENSv2 is required.
5. Do not invent contract addresses or interfaces.

NETWORK

ENSv2 writes for SAVIOURS are Sepolia only.

ENSv2 MUST be functional.
No hardcoded identity values in the final product.

SAVIOURS USE CASE

ENSv2 is the identity layer for security objects.

Example:

incident-00017.saviours.eth

The ENS identity should resolve to real machine-readable incident
metadata and/or security records.

ENS MUST NOT be cosmetic.

GOOD:
Threat incident
→ persistent registry
→ ENSv2 identity
→ resolver metadata
→ future agent retrieves incident identity

BAD:
Display ".eth" next to an incident as decoration.

WRITE SAFETY

AI must never directly perform ENS state mutation.

Application code must:
- validate inputs
- verify target/state
- perform deterministic transaction construction
- record transaction/result
- expose failure clearly

When registering a threat identity:

1. Register the ENSv2 subname.
2. Capture the resulting node identity/hash.
3. Persist that identity in the security registry.
4. Verify resolution.

Before coding, report:

### ENSv2 docs consulted
### Network/deployment verified
### Registry interface verified
### Resolver interface verified
### Access-control model verified
### Why ENSv2 is central to SAVIOURS
